WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.269
Jujutsu

00:00:01.447 --> 00:00:02.873
version control without

00:00:02.685 --> 00:00:03.911
Git's sharp edges

00:00:04.446 --> 00:00:05.837
Ethan Lowman's primer

00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:07.111
introduces jj to

00:00:06.922 --> 00:00:07.806
Git users

00:00:07.946 --> 00:00:08.877
It works side

00:00:08.688 --> 00:00:09.502
by side with

00:00:09.313 --> 00:00:09.914
Git in the

00:00:09.726 --> 00:00:11.341
same repository so

00:00:11.153 --> 00:00:11.813
you can try

00:00:11.625 --> 00:00:12.344
it today

00:00:12.886 --> 00:00:14.242
Automatic rebasing

00:00:14.053 --> 00:00:15.126
and native undo

00:00:14.938 --> 00:00:16.105
soften Git's sharp

00:00:15.917 --> 00:00:16.565
edges

00:00:16.624 --> 00:00:17.756
and make stacked-diff

00:00:17.568 --> 00:00:18.711
workflows easy

00:00:19.238 --> 00:00:20.405
Each change keeps

00:00:20.217 --> 00:00:21.242
a stable change

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:21.997
ID even as

00:00:21.809 --> 00:00:22.752
its commit hash

00:00:22.563 --> 00:00:23.282
changes

00:00:23.448 --> 00:00:24.756
so rewriting or

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.936
editing history never

00:00:25.747 --> 00:00:26.608
loses track of

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.138
your work

00:00:27.678 --> 00:00:28.692
Full story on

00:00:28.503 --> 00:00:29.399
the dashboard
